      "id": "variant:yosoi::ResponseTermination::Cancelled",
      "publicPath": "yosoi::ResponseTermination::Cancelled",
      "title": "yosoi::ResponseTermination::Cancelled",
      "kind": "variant",
      "signature": "Cancelled",
      "docs": "Execution observed caller cancellation before or during an acquisition.\n\nOutcomes already recorded remain available in [`Response::attempts`];\nthey are not rolled back. Every subsequent acquisition is represented as\nnot started with [`super::NotStartedReason::Cancelled`]. A token already\ncancelled when execution begins produces this result even for an empty\nacquisition sequence. This describes observed cancellation, not a promise\nthat every underlying external side effect was undone.",
      "source": {
        "file": "crates/yosoi/src/internal/engine/request/execution/outcome/response.rs",
        "lineStart": 96,
